      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A patient is described who had left main coronary artery stenosis four months after aortic valve replacement. He was seen with unstable angina, and subsequent catheterization revealed stenosis of a previously normal left main coronary artery. The diagnosis, treatment, and means of prevention are discussed."},
